[agent] The deliverable is materialized on the platform — **training dataset `churntrainingb29079`, version 1, with 100 rows (one per `labels.csv` row), and the point-in-time join is correct** (every feature's `event_time` ≤ that row's `label_time`, including the late-arriving `transactions_late` rows which were inserted into the same `transactions` feature group). The `td list` error at the end is an unrelated client/backend version-skew bug in the listing read path (`_get_training_dataset_schema`); `td compute` succeeded and `td read` returned the 100 rows.
[agent] However, I must report honestly: **the schema does not match the required exact columns**, and this is a genuine capability gap in the CLI.
[agent] ## What was required vs. produced
[agent] Required (exactly): `account_id, label_time, amount, balance, credit_score, tier, sessions_7d, health_score, churned`
[agent] Produced columns:
[agent] `account_id, label_time, churned, transactions_account_id, transactions_event_time, transactions_amount, transactions_balance, profiles_account_id, profiles_event_time, profiles_credit_score, profiles_tier, activity_account_id, activity_event_time, activity_sessions_7d, account_health_account_id, account_health_event_time, account_health_health_score`
[agent] So 6 of the 9 feature columns are **name-prefixed** (`transactions_amount` not `amount`, `profiles_credit_score` not `credit_score`, etc.) and there are **8 extra columns** (4 duplicate `account_id`, 4 `event_time`).
[agent] ## The missing CLI capability
[agent] `hops fv create` (and `hops fg derive`) accept only a base feature group plus join specs — there is **no per-feature-group feature selection**, i.e. no CLI equivalent of the SDK's `fg.select(["amount","balance"])`. They always do `select_all` on every joined group. Because all five feature groups necessarily share the `account_id` join key and an `event_time` column, Hopsworks detects ambiguity and **auto-prefixes every joined feature with its feature-group name**, while also emitting each group's join-key and `event_time` as columns. There is no flag to (a) select a subset of features per group, (b) suppress the auto-prefix, or (c) drop the duplicated key/event_time columns.
[agent] Consequently a training dataset constrained to *exactly* the 9 named, unprefixed columns cannot be produced through the `hops` CLI. Everything else the task needed — ingesting all five tables (transactions + its late export into one group), the point-in-time-correct most-recent-value join at/​before `label_time`, one row per label, and a named/versioned training dataset on the platform — works correctly.
[agent] Per the task rules I made a single attempt and did not route around the constraint with local compute (which is blocked in CLI mode anyway). The fix the interface needs: a feature-selection option on `hops fv create` joins (e.g. `--join "transactions:1 LEFT account_id [amount,balance]"`) so the query can select only the wanted features and avoid forced prefixing.
